# Production environment.
#
# Same-origin, deliberately. On the EC2 instance Nginx serves Fresko's static
# `dist/` and proxies `/api/` to Heimdall on 127.0.0.1:8000 (Heimdall binds to
# loopback only — see its README). Because both are the same origin there is no
# CORS, no preflight, and no hostname here to go stale.
#
# This was `https://phitv2.phit.b.com`, which does not resolve. Every data-driven
# surface — blog, innovation hub, services, careers, contact — failed in a
# production build while dev kept working, because dev points at localhost:8000.
# `vite.config.ts` now fails the build on a placeholder value so that cannot recur.
#
# Point this at an absolute origin ONLY if Fresko is ever served from a different
# host than the API. Then Heimdall must also be given a CORS allow-list.
VITE_API_URL=/

# Public origin the site is actually served from — used only to build absolute
# canonical/OG/Twitter URLs in src/shared/seo.ts (crawlers need an absolute
# URL there; a relative one is broken, not just non-ideal). This is NOT the
# same knob as VITE_API_URL above, which is same-origin `/` and carries no
# hostname. Value matches <PUBLIC_DOMAIN> in ../SETUP.md.
VITE_SITE_URL=https://phitopolis.com
